    "field": "climate change",
    "problem": "The paper addresses the uninvestigated differences in future Arctic warming amplification between various emission scenarios, a crucial gap for understanding how climate mitigation pathways affect the long-term rate of polar warming and the persistence of the ice-albedo feedback.",
    "method": "The authors use 50-member large-ensemble simulations from a single climate model, supported by multi-model analyses, to compare Arctic warming amplification and its relationship with sea-ice reduction and surface energy budgets between a low- and high-emission future scenario.",
    "task": "The task is to investigate why Arctic warming amplification is stronger in a future low-emission scenario compared to a high-emission one, using large-ensemble and multi-model climate simulations to analyze the role of sea-ice loss and associated feedback mechanisms.",
